%description:

Tcp.synRetries:active -- the SYN goes this many times again, and then the open fails.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "the retransmissions of a SYN or of a SYN-ACK, after which the open
fails".

The classes: retries (1 and more; 12 is the default, 6 the value of LinuxTcp), with a facet for
the SYN of an active open and one for the SYN-ACK of a passive open; zero (0). The code:
TcpConnection::process_TIMEOUT_SYN_REXMIT() gives up when the count of retransmissions
exceeds the value. This test separates the facet from "zero": with 0, the
SYN goes only once.

Host under test: host1, the active opener; the tap drops each SYN of host1. Observation:
level 1, three SYNs of host1 (the first and two retransmissions), and level 1 at the
application: the open fails, after the timeouts of 1, 2 and 4 s.

%# parameter: Tcp.synRetries
%# class: active
%# value: 2
%# key: *.host1.tcp.synRetries
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpTestApp.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpSynRetriesActive")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true").drop()
                     .describe("every SYN of host1"))
        .act(action().at(0.1).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) {
            app.socket().connect(app.addressOf("host2"), 1000);
        }))
        .meanwhile(exactlyTimes(3, on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                                       .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
                                       .describe("a SYN of host1")
                                       .within(9.0)))
        .once(on("host1.app[0]").signal("socketFailure")
                  .notBefore(6.9)
                  .describe("the failure of the open")
                  .within(7.1));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpSynRetriesActive compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.synRetries = 2    # the parameter under test
*.host1.app[0].typename = "TcpTestApp"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpSynRetriesActive: PASS
